Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DSH_PACKAGE@ (>= @DSH_MIN_VERSION@)
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Homepage: @PLUGIN_REPO_URL@
X-DSH-Plugin-Name: @PLUGIN_NAME@
X-DSH-Plugin-Version: @PLUGIN_VERSION@
X-DSH-Plugin-Commit: @PLUGIN_COMMIT@
Description: project and user-global memory for DeepSeek Harness
 Adds a per-project memory index and a cross-project user-global memory layer
 to DeepSeek Harness. Each session receives the MEMORY.md index as one
 injected context message, and eight tools maintain the store: memory_write,
 memory_read, memory_search, memory_delete, memory_audit, memory_sweep,
 memory_restore, and memory_dream.
 .
 The Web client adds an expandable Chat row for each injection and a /memory
 panel that lists, edits, archives, restores, and tidies notes through an
 owner-only route. Notes are plain markdown under $DSH_HOME/memory/ and never
 appear in the repository.
 .
 Installs the plugin package root under @PLUGIN_INSTALL_DIR@.
 It does not modify any user profile. Enable it for a profile with:
 .
   dsh plugin --profile @PROFILE@ add @PLUGIN_INSTALL_DIR@
 .
 or add the same directory on the Plugins page in the Web UI.
 .
 The plugin is architecture-independent JavaScript and runs inside the
 Harness Host process with the profile user's privileges.
